      "lineNbr": 351,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-11-16T01:46:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The is_{sys,ec}_rst_asserted() functions mean \"We\u0027re driving these signals to an asserted state ourselves\", not \"The GPIOs are asserted externally\". If we\u0027re driving them on purpose, we don\u0027t want the interrupt handlers to take any action.\n\nIt\u0027s not rebooting here, but it is requesting tpm_reset() before we\u0027re ready for it. If it doesn\u0027t do anything right away, it\u0027s only because the task priorities happen to prevent it. I want to ensure that it doesn\u0027t fire early even if someone rearranges the lines in ec.tasklist",
      "parentUuid": "30b088be_c888fd0a",
      "revId": "16b0675481c26242925db43b44d5b4cadf99fccb",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
